        "anchorX": 0.5,
        "anchorY": 1,
        "layer": "actorLayer",
        "zIndex": 2,
        "interaction": {
          "clickable": true,
          "hasInfo": false,
          "hasDrawer": true,
          "collectible": false,
          "bubbleMessage": "Ilove coffeee....",
          "infoModal": {
            "normal": {
              "title": "Coffee normal",
              "text": "Coffee normal text2",
              "imageSrc": "/assets/layout-info/mug-1786817023033.webp",
              "secondImageSrc": "/assets/layout-info/coffee-back-1786817030740.webp"
            }
          },
          "drawer": {
            "bodyHtml": "<p>I started out in Istanbul's agency scene as a junior designer with a tight deadline and a lot to prove, and somewhere between then and now the terminal won out over the canvas. Along the way I picked up two years in the Netherlands before landing in London, where I'm currently based. <br><br>That's the short version of how a design background turned into a development career.<br></p><p>These days most of my work is development. I still design when a project needs it, but I'm happiest deep in the code: Next.js, Webflow app development and Webflow Cloud, Supabase, DatoCMS, and HubSpot development, stitched into systems that are usually more complex under the hood than they look on screen.<br></p><p>My specialty is bringing Webflow and Shopify together: custom Shopify theme development and headless commerce builds that use Webflow's visual tooling without giving up the control a serious build needs. It's an unusual combination (most people live in one platform or the other, not both), and that's exactly why it's useful.<br></p><p>On the side, I've been building an AI-powered app that keeps an eye on Shopify competitors and turns what it finds into a weekly audio briefing, a good excuse to poke at OpenAI's API and a diff engine at the same time.<br></p><p>Outside of code: guitar (ten years in a band), an unreasonably competitive streak in fighting games, a cat with strong opinions about my desk chair, and an ongoing negotiation with my tomato plants.</p><p>I care about things that work properly and look like someone actually thought about them. That's the whole philosophy.</p>",
            "title": "About me"
          }
        }
